## Base letter

Dear Hiring Team,

I would like to apply for the [ROLE TITLE] role at [COMPANY].

The thing I have found about AI in practice is that it changes what one person can do, and I have been on both sides of that change. I was one of the leads developing the AI-enabled search APIs at ANZ Plus, on a generative AI platform built on Vertex AI and Gemini, owning technical design, model selection, and the practical guardrails a tier-one bank needs without compromising compliance or reliability. Before that I architected and led real-time, event-driven backend systems at Macquarie in Java and Spring Boot. I am hands-on first and I write a lot of code.

What I bring alongside the engineering is a genuine product and strategy head, and I am comfortable and practised at leading and growing teams. Beyond my paid roles I act as product manager for a mission-critical incident management system used across the country, recently authoring its national scaling strategy and presenting it to the national executive. I have led engineering teams through delivery and mentored engineers into the standards I set. Translating frontline needs into sound technical decisions, and lifting the people around me as I go, is just how I work. Outside paid work I keep building, most recently AccessBuddy, a multi-tenant SaaS I designed and shipped solo end to end.

[TAILOR — why this company and role. One short paragraph, one genuine reason grounded in what they actually do. Open with the constant: "My motivation has always been work with real impact." Then the company-specific reason, for example reach and consequence at scale, a domain where reliability really matters, or a team clearly investing in genuine engineering rather than gesture. If you have a referral, place it here: "[Name] spoke highly of the company and team, and his judgment is one I trust from working with him directly." Close the paragraph with: "That is the environment I want to be in."]

I look forward to the opportunity to discuss the role further.

Nicholas Wood
0427 081 551 | nicholas.h.wood@outlook.com

